<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The shock passing through the air above UMW_Earthshake's ground burst (AbilityDefs/Earthshake.xml,
       spawned by the vanilla CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget on that def). The stun itself rolls
       outward through the earth; this is the answering ripple overhead, reaching a little further than
       the stun does because air carries what soil damps.

       A deliberate self-contained COPY of the shipped distortion-wave recipe, following the same
       reasoning as FleckDefs/RallyingCryLightshaft.xml: the shipped instances
       (Core `ShockwaveFast`, Biotech `Fleck_BlastMechBandShockwave`, Royalty `PsychicApplyNeuroquake`)
       have no `Name=` so none can be a ParentName target, and their timings are tuned for effects an
       order of magnitude larger than a one-pawn slam. Everything referenced here is CORE-owned, so this
       needs no MayRequire despite the closest analog living in Biotech:
         • shaderType MoteLargeDistortionWave  - Core, Defs/Misc/ShaderTypeDefs/ShaderTypes.xml
         • Things/Mote/Black, PsychicDistortionCurrents, PsycastNoise
                                               - all three referenced by Core's own `ShockwaveFast`
       Mods cannot ship Unity shaders, so the only genuine screen-distortion available is one of the
       shaderTypes RimWorld already compiled in; this is that, not an imitation of it.

       Sizing (decompile-verified 2026-07-25, RimWorld 1.6). The rendered quad is drawSize * ExactScale
       world units square, and 1 world unit = 1 cell: Graphic_Fleck.DrawFleck multiplies the per-instance
       scale by graphicData.drawSize into the render matrix, over MeshPool's unit plane. FleckStatic starts
       linearScale at the spawn `scale` (1 here, the comp's default) and growthRate ADDS cells/second to
       it. So the outer edge finishes at:
           drawSize / 2 * (1 + growthRate * lifetime) = 6.0 / 2 * (1 + 1.5 * 0.40) = 4.8 cells
       against the ability's 3.9-cell stun radius, i.e. slightly wider, which is the intent. growthRate
       1.5 is Biotech's mech-band value; drawSize carries the rest so the pace stays vanilla's.

       Timing rides the ground burst: at the ability's propagationSpeed 0.3 the outermost stunned cell is
       reached at 18 ticks (0.30s), so a 0.40s ripple leads the roll out and outlives it by a beat rather
       than lingering after the shock has passed.

       _distortionIntensity 0.05 sits at the subtle end of the range shipped for THIS shader (Biotech's
       mech-band shockwave, the one physical stun shockwave in the game, is 0.066; Core's ShockwaveFast is
       0.2; Anomaly's quieter rings are 0.05) - raise toward 0.066 if it reads as too faint in play. Compare
       only within MoteLargeDistortionWave: the same number means something different under
       MoteGlowDistortBackground, which is what Core's PsycastAreaEffect uses.
       _brightnessMultiplier 1.15 is the value every shipped distortion-wave
       fleck uses. altitudeLayer MoteOverheadLow matches the mech-band shockwave and draws above pawns
       (Altitudes maps the enum in order, and MoteOverheadLow > Pawn) without climbing into the
       vision/overlay layers. drawOffscreen is deliberately absent: it only gates the EffecterDef +
       SubEffecter_Sprayer spawn path, and this spawns via FleckMaker, which never checks it.
       drawSize/growthRate/intensity are the eyeball-tunable knobs; see §7 of the spec for the in-game
       visual check, since the shader's internal ring-sweep timing cannot be read from a decompile. -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="FleckBase">
    <defName>UMW_EarthshakeRipple</defName>
    <altitudeLayer>MoteOverheadLow</altitudeLayer>
    <fadeInTime>0.04</fadeInTime>
    <solidTime>0.26</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>0.10</fadeOutTime> <!-- lifetime 0.40s; see the sizing note above -->
    <growthRate>1.5</growthRate>
    <graphicData>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_FleckPulse</graphicClass> <!-- feeds AgeSecs to the shader; the ring sweep needs it -->
      <texPath>Things/Mote/Black</texPath>
      <shaderType>MoteLargeDistortionWave</shaderType>
      <shaderParameters>
        <_DistortionTex>/Things/Mote/PsychicDistortionCurrents</_DistortionTex>
        <_NoiseTex>/Things/Mote/PsycastNoise</_NoiseTex>
        <_distortionIntensity>0.05</_distortionIntensity>
        <_brightnessMultiplier>1.15</_brightnessMultiplier>
      </shaderParameters>
      <drawSize>6.0</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

</Defs>
